config BR2_PACKAGE_SPINAND
	bool "W25N02KV SPI-NAND: 32 MiB UBIFS data volume"
	depends on !BR2_PACKAGE_SDCARD
	depends on !BR2_PACKAGE_GALLERY_SDCARD
	help
	  Enable a Winbond W25N02KV on SPI5 and expose the first 32 MiB as
	  an UBI-managed UBIFS data volume. The package applies the required
	  Linux and BusyBox configuration fragments, builds a dedicated DTB,
	  and installs the spinand-ubi setup/status helper.

	  SPI5 clock and data are shared with the onboard gyroscope, LCD
	  controller, and optional W5500. SPI-NAND uses its own PG3 chip select.
	  The SD card remains isolated on SPI4. NAND is never erased or formatted
	  automatically. Run
	  "spinand-ubi format --yes" once after checking the wiring.

	  See package/spinand/README.md for wiring and first-use instructions.

if BR2_PACKAGE_SPINAND

menu "W25N02KV SPI-NAND options"

config BR2_PACKAGE_SPINAND_COMPRESS_INITRAMFS
	bool "Compress the initramfs with gzip"
	default y
	help
	  Store the embedded root filesystem as a gzip-compressed archive in
	  internal flash. Linux expands it into RAM during boot; the kernel
	  remains an XIP image and continues executing directly from flash.

	  SPI-NAND support adds MTD, UBI, UBIFS, and management utilities, so
	  compression is enabled by default to help the final xipImage stay
	  below the STM32F429 project's 2,048,000-byte limit.

config BR2_PACKAGE_SPINAND_AUTOMOUNT
	bool "Mount an initialized UBIFS volume automatically at boot"
	default y
	help
	  Probe the W25N02KV during boot, attach its UBI partition, and mount
	  the data volume at /mnt/spinand. Existing data is never erased.

	  When the NAND is detected but has no usable UBI data volume, boot
	  prints the explicit one-time initialization command:
	  "spinand-ubi format --yes". Formatting remains a manual destructive
	  action and is never performed by this option.

config BR2_PACKAGE_SPINAND_FASTMAP
	bool "Use UBI fastmap checkpoints (experimental)"
	default n
	help
	  Enable Linux CONFIG_MTD_UBI_FASTMAP and request automatic fastmap
	  creation before UBI is attached. The first attach still performs a
	  full scan and writes a checkpoint; later attaches can restore the UBI
	  mapping by reading the fastmap instead of scanning every eraseblock.

	  Linux 6.6 marks the on-flash fastmap format experimental. Fastmap also
	  reserves eraseblocks for two checkpoint copies. Back up an existing
	  volume before enabling this option: volumes created with "ubimkvol -m"
	  may need to be reformatted so those eraseblocks can be reserved.

endmenu

endif

comment "W25N02KV SPI-NAND is unavailable with SD card (storage image size)"
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_SDCARD

comment "W25N02KV SPI-NAND is unavailable with Gallery SD support (storage image size)"
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_GALLERY_SDCARD
